      <div class="f-copy">
        
          <h3 class="f-name">Nishit<br>
<em>Ratthe</em></h3>
        

        
          <p class="f-moment">I love beauty too much to watch it swim in mediocrity.</p>
        

        
          <div class="f-bio"><p>Fourteen years at L'Oréal and Marico, spent falling deeply in love with what beauty could actually do. Nishit has always believed the category holds something close to magic: real science, world-class ingredients, the genuine power to change how someone feels in their own skin. His whole career has been about chasing that potential rather than the shortcut. Beauty taught him more about life than anything else, and he wanted to give that back in a product that earns its claims. For him, longevity was never a trend to ride. It is the most honest expression of what skincare is for: not fixing you, but supporting what your skin can already become, kept up long enough to last.</p></div>
        
      </div>

      
    </div>
  
    <div class="f nb">
      

      <div class="f-copy">
        
          <h3 class="f-name">Pratha<br>
<em>Bhatia</em></h3>
        

        
          <p class="f-moment">I know what it costs to not feel like yourself. And I know a daily habit can give it back.</p>
        

        
          <div class="f-bio"><p>Parsons-trained. Rejected an offer from The MET, left NYC to come back and build in India. Pratha has always seen creation as a place of possibility, where something made well can change how a person carries themselves. She believes in the value of looking good, and in the craft of making things genuinely beautiful, not because surface is everything, but because it isn't nothing. Her real subject is confidence. Having spent years on the wrong side of it herself, she understands that confidence is rarely a feeling you wait for. It is built, slowly, through the small things you do for yourself every day. LNGVTY is that idea in a bottle: a daily habit, kept long enough to become a different way of seeing yourself.</p></div>
        
      </div>

      
